\describe{
\item{\code{feature}}{string; never \code{NA}. As given on stdin.}
\item{\code{studies}}{int; in \strong{tests}; never \code{NA}. Tests combined: mzLib's CombinedPValue.Studies, the finite p-values after any signed conversion.}
\item{\code{omitted}}{int; in \strong{tests}; never \code{NA}. This feature's lines that were not combined: a blank, NA or NaN p_value, or (signed) an effect that is 0, blank, NA or NaN. studies + omitted is the feature's line count.}
\item{\code{statistic}}{float; in \strong{fisher: chi-square statistic on 2 x studies degrees of freedom; stouffer: standard normal deviates}; \code{NA} when not finite. With studies 0, nothing was combined (p_value null too). Otherwise p_value says which: 0 means plus infinity (a p-value of 0 among the tests), 1 means minus infinity (stouffer, a p-value of 1), and null means undefined (stouffer, a p-value of 0 and one of 1 together). Fisher's X = -2 sum ln p, or Stouffer's Z = sum w z / sqrt(sum w^2).}
\item{\code{p_value}}{float; in \strong{fraction (0 to 1)}; \code{NA} when studies is 0 (nothing to combine), or stouffer met a p-value of 0 and one of 1 (z of plus and minus infinity). Combined p-value: the UPPER tail of the statistic's reference distribution, so it tests one direction (effect > 0 when signed). Fisher's is the regularized upper incomplete gamma Q(k, X/2), so a tiny value keeps its digits. Not adjusted across features.}
}
